.TH SDL_arraysize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_arraysize \- The number of elements in a static array.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_arraysize(array) (sizeof(array)/sizeof(array[0]))  /* or `_Countof(array)` on recent gcc and clang */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This will compile but return incorrect results for a pointer to an array; it has to be an array the compiler knows the size of\[char46]
.PP
This macro looks like it double-evaluates the argument, but it does so inside of
.BR sizeof ,
so there are no side-effects here, as expressions do not actually run any code in these cases\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

